; The Sega CD Model 2's extension spacer and its plate, a primitive stand-in in the
; DRIVE's frame (sega_cd2_primitive.gd: +X right, +Y up, +Z front, y = 0 under the
; drive's feet, x = 0 the middle of its plan), so its origin is the drive's shell
; origin and an identity GrabPoint seats it at the drive's AccessoryMount. Figures:
; RetroXR-models sega/sega-cd/console-2-spacer params.py (auction photographs scaled
; by the drive, the service manual's drawing; LOW confidence): the bar 52 out from the
; platform's left end (x -250.5 to -198.1: the patent's -243 to -190.6, moved 7.5 left
; with the base's end when the drive took Sega's published 396 width), the drive's depth less its corners, its top
; level with the rim (45); the platform's two rails carried on as slots; seven ribs
; down its outer face; the steel plate under both (84 x 100); two rubber feet.
[node name="SegaCd2Spacer" type="RigidBody3D"]
collision_layer = 4
collision_mask = 196613
mass = 0.12
physics_material_override = SubResource("PhysMat_spacer")
freeze_mode = 1
linear_damp = 5.0
angular_damp = 8.0
script = ExtResource("1_spacer")

